In a math contest, fix an integer base c = {base_c} with c > 1. Define A = c^{exp_m} and B = c^{exp_n}, where exp_m and exp_n are distinct positive integers. Consider the system of equations:
  log_A x + log_B y = {sum_s}
  log_x A - log_y B = {diff_t}
This system has exactly two real solutions (x1, y1) and (x2, y2) with x1, x2, y1, y2 > 0 and each logarithm well-defined (all bases positive and not equal to 1). Compute the value of log_{c^{base_r}}(x1 y1 x2 y2).

